-----------Let & Const Work Differently In Variable Declaration, Assignment, Reassignment-----------
    The let keyword allows you to declare variables that can be updated or reassigned later (flexible container).

let score = 10;
console.log(score);
>>> 10
score = 20;
console.log(score);
>>> 20

    The const keyword is used to declare variables that are constant. Once you assign a value to a variable declared with const, you cannot reassign it.

const maxScore = 100;
console.log(maxScore); // 100
maxScore = 200; // This will result in an error

